messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 612 and 482?I think the correct answer is: 284984\n', "<think>\nTo find the product of 612 and 482, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 612 as 600 plus 12, and 482 as 400 plus 82.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This means I'll calculate 600 times 400, 600 times 82, 12 times 400, and 12 times 82.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **612** and **482**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n612 = 600 + 12\n\\]\n\\[\n482 = 400 + 82\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n612 \\times 482 = (600 + 12) \\times (400 + 82)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 600 \\times 400 + 600 \\times 82 + 12 \\times 400 + 12 \\times 82\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(600 \\times 400\\)**\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 400 = 240,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(600 \\times 82\\)**\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 82 = 49,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(12 \\times 400\\)**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 400 = 4,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(12 \\times 82\\)**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 82 = 984\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n240,\\!000 + 49,\\!200 + 4,\\!800 + 984 = 294,\\!984\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{294,\\!984}\n\\].Therefore, the answer is"]]
