messages:   31%|###       | 154/500 [00:26<00:34, 10.12it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 260 and 305?I think the correct answer is: 79307\n', "<think>\nTo find the product of 260 and 305, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 260 as 200 plus 60, and 305 as 300 plus 5.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 260 by each part of 305.\n\nThis will give me four separate multiplication problems: 200 times 300, 200 times 5, 60 times 300, and 60 times 5.\n\nAfter calculating each of these, I'll add all the results together to find the final product.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **260** and **305**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n260 = 200 + 60\n\\]\n\\[\n305 = 300 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n260 \\times 305 = (200 + 60) \\times (300 + 5)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 200 \\times 300 + 200 \\times 5 + 60 \\times 300 + 60 \\times 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(200 \\times 300\\)**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 300 = 60,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(200 \\times 5\\)**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 5 = 1,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(60 \\times 300\\)**\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 300 = 18,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(60 \\times 5\\)**\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 5 = 300\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Results Together\n\n\\[\n60,\\!000 + 1,\\!000 + 18,\\!000 + 300 = 79,\\!300\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{79,\\!300}\n\\].Therefore, the answer is"]]
