messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 375 and 775?I think the correct answer is: 296625\n', "<think>\nTo find the product of 375 and 775, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 375 as 300 + 70 + 5 and 775 as 700 + 70 + 5.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 375 by each part of 775. This means I'll calculate:\n\n300 × 700 = 210,000  \n300 × 70 = 21,000  \n300 × 5 = 1,500  \n70 × 700 = 49,000  \n70 × 70 = 4,900  \n70 × 5 = 350  \n5 × 700 = 3,500  \n5 × 70 = 350  \n5 × 5 = 25\n\nAfter calculating all these products, I'll add them together to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **375** and **775**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number in expanded form to make multiplication easier.\n\n\\[\n375 = 300 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n775 = 700 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nUse the distributive property to multiply each part of **375** by each part of **775**.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n300 \\times 700 &= 210,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 70 &= 21,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 5 &= 1,\\!500 \\\\\n70 \\times 700 &= 49,\\!000 \\\\\n70 \\times 70 &= 4,\\!900 \\\\\n70 \\times 5 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 700 &= 3,\\!500 \\\\\n5 \\times 70 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 5 &= 25 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results from the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n210,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 49,\\!000 + 4,\\!900 + 350 + 3,\\!500 + 350 + 25 = 306,\\!250\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{306,\\!250}\n\\].Therefore, the answer is"]]
