messages:   45%|####5     | 227/500 [00:36<00:30,  8.96it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 220 and 776?I think the correct answer is: 100720\n', "<think>\nTo find the product of 220 and 776, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 220 as 200 + 20 and 776 as 700 + 70 + 6.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 220 by each part of 776.\n\nThis will give me several multiplication steps: 200 multiplied by 700, 200 multiplied by 70, 200 multiplied by 6, 20 multiplied by 700, 20 multiplied by 70, and 20 multiplied by 6.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n\nFinally, I'll sum all these values to find the total product of 220 and 776.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **220** and **776**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\n\\[\n220 \\times 776 = (200 + 20) \\times (700 + 70 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nNow, multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n200 \\times 700 &= 140,\\!000 \\\\\n200 \\times 70 &= 14,\\!000 \\\\\n200 \\times 6 &= 1,\\!200 \\\\\n20 \\times 700 &= 14,\\!000 \\\\\n20 \\times 70 &= 1,\\!400 \\\\\n20 \\times 6 &= 120 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nSum all the results from the previous step.\n\n\\[\n140,\\!000 + 14,\\!000 + 1,\\!200 + 14,\\!000 + 1,\\!400 + 120 = 170,\\!720\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{170,\\!720}\n\\].Therefore, the answer is"]]
