messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 851 and 816?I think the correct answer is: 694516\n', "<think>\nTo find the product of 851 and 816, I'll start by breaking down each number into smaller, more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll express 851 as 800 plus 50 plus 1. Similarly, I'll express 816 as 800 plus 16.\n\nNext, I'll multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This involves calculating eight separate products: 800 times 800, 800 times 16, 50 times 800, 50 times 16, 1 times 800, 1 times 16, and so on.\n\nAfter calculating all these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that I don't miss any components and helps in accurately computing the total product.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **851** and **816**, we'll use the **standard multiplication algorithm**. Here's a step-by-step solution:.\n\n### Step 1: Write the Numbers Vertically.\n\n```.\n   851.\n×  816.\n--------.\n```.\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 851 by Each Digit of 816.\n\n1. **Multiply by 6 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   851 \\times 6 = 5106.\n   \\].\n   .\n2. **Multiply by 10 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   851 \\times 10 = 8510 \\quad (\\text{Shift one position to the left}).\n   \\].\n   .\n3. **Multiply by 800 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   851 \\times 800 = 680800 \\quad (\\text{Shift two positions to the left}).\n   \\].\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n& \\quad \\,\\,\\, 5106 \\\\.\n& + \\,\\, 85100 \\\\.\n& + 680800 \\\\.\n\\hline.Therefore, the answer is"]]
